{
  "_doc": "Neighbourhood profiles for DistrictGen (loosely after Night City in the Time of the Red). pattern: grid | organic | radial. block: [min, max] block size in squares. road_w: road width incl. sidewalks. diag/curve: chance of a diagonal avenue / curved road on top. alley: chance a lot split leaves a 2-wide alley. floors/security/decay: [min, max] ranges for non-target buildings (floors capped by the scene). cars: parked-car density; wreck_ratio: share of those that are wrecks. mix: weights over building site types and outdoor lots (market, park, plaza, parking_lot, rubble_field, substation). target: site type of the gig target. Optional (theme parks, after real park plans: a hub plaza with lands off it, wide pedestrian midways, fenced ride enclosures with queue benches, kiosks along the walks, a boardwalk on the sea): midway (roads are paved walks, not asphalt), hub (the lot at a radial pattern's centre becomes this yard), shore (a boardwalk and the sea along the bottom edge), street_props {rate, pieces} (what stands along the walks, instead of the city's vending machines and benches), pockets (what the leftover small lots become, instead of park/plaza/parking); the outdoor lots `ride` (a fenced ride enclosure with one gate) and `woods` (a dense stand of trees: the Haunted Woods' fake forest). Theme parks also take (ParkGen): midway_props {rate, pieces, string_spacing} (game booths and kiosks along the walks' edges, strings of lights on poles across them every string_spacing squares, 0 = none), pier (a pier off the boardwalk with the big wheel on it) and sea_div (sea depth = map height / sea_div), ground (the open ground between lots, default sidewalk: a wood's is grass), path / verge (the walks' middle and edge: a wood's earth paths between grass verges), forest (share of open grass that gets a tree: the Haunted Woods' fake pines); ride lots get a ride (big wheel, coaster, carousel, bumper cars, spinner, swings, drop tower) and a queue lane. look: a profile's own district look, worn over the gig district's (DistrictLook.of_params: its keys win, its mats/light/walls merge entry by entry).",
